\tag{decision}
\tag{area:rt}
\tag{status:provisional}

\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{\code{ReedyFibrant P} is an explicit property for the proved shape model. A chosen functorial \code{R_rd} must preserve reduced object labels and yield a \code{LevelEq} \code{P → R_rd P}, with the corresponding boundary and Segal conditions. Its existence is \ref{at-kr-0011}. If the chosen shapes do not make all sources cofibrant, relative mapping constructions also specify a cofibrant source replacement. Any categorical replacement is named separately. Standard objects have only the fibrancy certificates actually proved.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{Relative mapping invariance uses a specified weak equivalence class.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rejected}
  \p{Claiming Reedy replacement alone implements categorical localization.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Acceptance}
  \p{\ref{at-kr-0011}, \ref{at-fd-0003}, \ref{at-fd-0008}.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{provisional until the chosen diagram model is validated.}
}
